        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done. The spectrum (`/app/graphene.dat`, comma-decimal, tab-separated) was loaded and both graphene peaks fitted with Lorentzian profiles `L(x) = A·γ²/((x−x₀)²+γ²) + offset` (γ = HWHM):\n\n**G peak** (fit window 3650–3870 cm⁻¹, incl. local linear background, R² ≈ 0.995):\n- x₀ ≈ 3744.87 cm⁻¹, γ ≈ 26.70 cm⁻¹, amplitude ≈ 12660 (peak height), offset ≈ 727\n\n**2D peak** (center ~19205–19235 cm⁻¹; the top of this peak is detector-saturated at ~79400 counts, so the fit used the wings plus unsaturated points):\n- x₀ ≈ 19204.7 cm⁻¹, γ ≈ 244.5 cm⁻¹, amplitude ≈ 106377 (extrapolated peak height, consistent with the saturated maximum), offset ≈ 16009 (local baseline)\n\nResults written to **/app/results.json** in the requested format:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"G\":  {\"x0\": 3744.87,  \"gamma\": 26.70,  \"amplitude\": 12659.82,   \"offset\": 726.94},\n  \"2D\": {\"x0\": 19204.69, \"gamma\": 244.49, \"amplitude\": 106377.29, \"offset\": 16008.81}\n}\n```\n\nNote: the file's x-axis appears to be in an unusual unit scale (G at ~3745 instead of ~1580 cm⁻¹ — a factor of ~2.36), but the fit was performed directly on the given axis values.",
